, a late-August poll showing the candidates separated by a single point, and endorsements of Kirschner from two Manatee County Republicans point to at least some cross-pressure. An independent candidate trails far behind. Gruters is expected to win by about five points, with meaningful uncertainty remaining.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.257, "margin": -3.74}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.2349, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.1906, "margin": -6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.2331, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.1854, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.1943, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.2766, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.2403, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.2304, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.1856, "margin": -6.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.2293, "margin": -5.0}]}